Modifications from the original (2026):
- Removed external plugin resolution (resolve-companion.sh-equivalent lookup);
  the engine ships as part of this plugin rather than being resolved from a
  separately-installed "codex@openai-codex" plugin.
- Renamed internal env var prefix CODEX_COMPANION_* to CODEX_KIT_*.
- Model/effort persistence to ~/.codex/config.toml changed from always-on to
  opt-in (--persist flag), with per-call flags as the default.
- Added sandbox-mode viability testing and explicit non-silent fallback
  reporting to `setup`.
- Added independent double-check verification, document/plan verification,
  research, a generic reviewer-agnostic bridge, and other components not
  present in the original.

---

scripts/lib/codex-exec.mjs's Windows `.cmd`/`.bat` shim-spawning support
(`escapeWindowsCommand`, `escapeWindowsArgument`, and the invocation-building
logic in `buildSpawnInvocation`) is a direct port of `cross-spawn`'s Windows
argument-escaping algorithm (https://github.com/moxystudio/node-cross-spawn).

